          "id": "effd8c1db67b10dad2054adbc2446a16889e101f",
          "message": "Update path to `data/test_config.yaml` (#118)\n\nThis PR resolves the test failures in `tests/test_utils.py` that look\r\nlike:\r\n\r\n```\r\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: './data/test_config.yaml'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe error occurs because the upstream `vllm` project runs tests using\r\nthe `tests` directory as the working directory, but we use the project\r\nroot as the working directory. Perhaps that directory is used upstream\r\nto avoid the issue with being in the project root and having a folder\r\nnamed `vllm` that impacts the import system.\r\n\r\nUnless we want to adjust our test run config to also run using the\r\n`tests` folder as the working directory, this PR seems like the smallest\r\nchange to correct the tests (as such, I’ve added the “UPSTREAM SYNC”\r\ncomments so it can be maintained).",
